IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `s121-nouns`
IMPORT `s121-support`
IMPORT `s121-a-exclusion`
IMPORT `s121-b-limitations`
IMPORT `s121-c-reduced`
IMPORT `s121-d1-special`
IMPORT `s121-d9-service`
IMPORT `s121-efg`

-- 26 U.S.C. section 121. LAYER 1, module 9: the whole section, assembled from the rules of the other modules.
-- Nothing is restated here: every rule of the section is called from its own module, and this module only puts the calls in the order the text gives.
-- The order is the text's own cross-references:
--   (1) the gates that take the sale out of the section: (d)(5)(A) the event, (e), (f), (d)(10), (d)(8);
--   (2) each individual's holding, with (d)(2) to (d)(5)(C), (d)(7) and (g) applied, over the 5-year period of (a), as extended by (d)(9) or (d)(12);
--   (3) the route: (a), with (d)(1) for a joint return and (b)(3) for an earlier sale, or else (c);
--   (4) the limitation: (b)(1), (b)(2) or (b)(4), reduced by (c)(1) on the (c) route;
--   (5) the gain: less the gain of (d)(6), less the gain allocated to nonqualified use by (b)(5), as (b)(5)(D) orders;
--   (6) the amount excluded: the smaller of the gain left and the limitation, as (b)(1) says "shall not exceed".
-- Where one rule's answer is NOTHING (not covered) the answer built on it is NOTHING: nothing here turns NOTHING into FALSE.
-- The two places the text does not say whose facts to use on a joint return are forks F16 and F17 in NOTES.md.
-- Whose service suspends the 5-year period, and on which returns, is fork F30: the electing individual's own and the spouse's, on any return.

-- The provisions this module assembles, quoted mechanically from the text so that the locators below can be checked against it (srcrefs.py).
-- The quotations stand for the whole of each range cited; where a locator spans more lines than are quoted here, the ends are quoted and the module that encodes the middle quotes it in full.
-- src:13 | (a) Exclusion
-- src:14 | Gross income shall not include gain from the sale or exchange of property if, during the 5-year period ending on the date of the sale or exchange, such property has been owned and used by the taxpayer as the taxpayer’s principal residence for periods aggregating 2 years or more.
-- src:16 | (1) In general
-- src:17 | The amount of gain excluded from gross income under subsection (a) with respect to any sale or exchange shall not exceed $250,000.
-- src:26 | If such spouses do not meet the requirements of subparagraph (A), the limitation under paragraph (1) shall be the sum of the limitations under paragraph (1) to which each spouse would be entitled if such spouses had not been married. For purposes of the preceding sentence, each spouse shall be treated as owning the property during the period that either spouse owned the property.
-- src:27 | (3) Application to only 1 sale or exchange every 2 years
-- src:28 | Subsection (a) shall not apply to any sale or exchange by the taxpayer if, during the 2-year period ending on the date of such sale or exchange, there was any other sale or exchange by the taxpayer to which subsection (a) applied.
-- src:29 | (4) Special rule for certain sales by surviving spouses
-- src:30 | In the case of a sale or exchange of property by an unmarried individual whose spouse is deceased on the date of such sale, paragraph (1) shall be applied by substituting “$500,000” for “$250,000” if such sale occurs not later than 2 years after the date of death of such spouse and the requirements of paragraph (2)(A) were met immediately before such date of death.
-- src:69 | (2) Property of deceased spouse
-- src:70 | For purposes of this section, in the case of an unmarried individual whose spouse is deceased on the date of the sale or exchange of property, the period such unmarried individual owned and used such property shall include the period such deceased spouse owned and used such property before death.
-- src:71 | (3) Property owned by spouse or former spouse
-- src:72 | For purposes of this section—
-- src:73 | (A) Property transferred to individual from spouse or former spouse
-- src:74 | In the case of an individual holding property transferred to such individual in a transaction described in section 1041(a), the period such individual owns such property shall include the period the transferor owned the property.
-- src:75 | (B) Property used by former spouse pursuant to divorce decree, etc.
-- src:76 | Solely for purposes of this section, an individual shall be treated as using property as such individual’s principal residence during any period of ownership while such individual’s spouse or former spouse is granted use of the property under a divorce or separation instrument.
-- src:77 | (C) Divorce or separation instrument
-- src:78 | For purposes of this paragraph, the term “divorce or separation instrument” means—
-- src:79 | (i) a decree of divorce or separate maintenance or a written instrument incident to such a decree,
-- src:80 | (ii) a written separation agreement, or
-- src:81 | (iii) a decree (not described in clause (i)) requiring a spouse to make payments for the support or maintenance of the other spouse.
-- src:82 | (4) Tenant-stockholder in cooperative housing corporation
-- src:83 | For purposes of this section, if the taxpayer holds stock as a tenant-stockholder (as defined in section 216) in a cooperative housing corporation (as defined in such section), then—
-- src:84 | (A) the holding requirements of subsection (a) shall be applied to the holding of such stock, and
-- src:85 | (B) the use requirements of subsection (a) shall be applied to the house or apartment which the taxpayer was entitled to occupy as such stockholder.
-- src:86 | (5) Involuntary conversions
-- src:87 | (A) In general
-- src:88 | For purposes of this section, the destruction, theft, seizure, requisition, or condemnation of property shall be treated as the sale of such property.
-- src:89 | (B) Application of section 1033
-- src:90 | In applying section 1033 (relating to involuntary conversions), the amount realized from the sale or exchange of property shall be treated as being the amount determined without regard to this section, reduced by the amount of gain not included in gross income pursuant to this section.
-- src:91 | (C) Property acquired after involuntary conversion
-- src:92 | If the basis of the property sold or exchanged is determined (in whole or in part) under section 1033(b) (relating to basis of property acquired through involuntary conversion), then the holding and use by the taxpayer of the converted property shall be treated as holding and use by the taxpayer of the property sold or exchanged.
-- src:93 | (6) Recognition of gain attributable to depreciation
-- src:94 | Subsection (a) shall not apply to so much of the gain from the sale of any property as does not exceed the portion of the depreciation adjustments (as defined in section 1250(b)(3)) attributable to periods after May 6, 1997, in respect of such property.
-- src:95 | (7) Determination of use during periods of out-of-residence care
-- src:96 | In the case of a taxpayer who—
-- src:97 | (A) becomes physically or mentally incapable of self-care, and
-- src:98 | (B) owns property and uses such property as the taxpayer’s principal residence during the 5-year period described in subsection (a) for periods aggregating at least 1 year,
-- src:99 | then the taxpayer shall be treated as using such property as the taxpayer’s principal residence during any time during such 5-year period in which the taxpayer owns the property and resides in any facility (including a nursing home) licensed by a State or political subdivision to care for an individual in the taxpayer’s condition.
-- src:107 | (A) In general
-- src:108 | At the election of an individual with respect to a property, the running of the 5-year period described in subsections (a) and (c)(1)(B) and paragraph (7) of this subsection with respect to such property shall be suspended during any period that such individual or such individual’s spouse is serving on qualified official extended duty—
-- src:109 | (i) as a member of the uniformed services,
-- src:110 | (ii) as a member of the Foreign Service of the United States, or
-- src:111 | (iii) as an employee of the intelligence community.
-- src:112 | (B) Maximum period of suspension
-- src:113 | The 5-year period described in subsection (a) shall not be extended more than 10 years by reason of subparagraph (A).
-- src:155 | (g) Residences acquired in rollovers under section 1034
-- src:156 | For purposes of this section, in the case of property the acquisition of which by the taxpayer resulted under section 1034 [^1] (as in effect on the day before the date of the enactment of this section) in the nonrecognition of any part of the gain realized on the sale or exchange of another residence, in determining the period for which the taxpayer has owned and used such property as the taxpayer’s principal residence, there shall be included the aggregate periods for which such other residence (and each prior residence taken into account under section 1223(6) [^1] in determining the holding period of such property) had been so owned and used.

§ `The facts a sale is asked about`

-- What one individual states about the property and about themselves.
-- Each field is a fact the person can state; the borrowed terms of sections 216, 267(b), 707(b), 877(a)(1), 1033, 1034, 1041(a) and 1250(b)(3) are asked as facts.
DECLARE `Individual facts` HAS
    `holding of the property` IS A Holding
    `unmarried, spouse deceased on the date of the sale or exchange` IS A BOOLEAN
    `deceased spouse's holding of the property` IS A Holding
    `date of the spouse's death` IS A DATE
    `deceased spouse's dates of other sales or exchanges to which subsection (a) applied` IS A LIST OF DATE
    `property received in a transaction described in section 1041(a)` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the transferor's periods of ownership` IS A LIST OF Span
    `uses granted to a spouse or former spouse` IS A LIST OF `Use granted`
    `tenant-stockholder in a cooperative housing corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
    `periods of holding the stock` IS A LIST OF Span
    `periods of occupying the house or apartment` IS A LIST OF Span
    `basis of the property sold determined under section 1033(b)` IS A BOOLEAN
    `holding of the converted property` IS A Holding
    `became physically or mentally incapable of self-care` IS A BOOLEAN
    `stays in facilities` IS A LIST OF `Stay in a facility`
    `acquired under section 1034 in a rollover` IS A BOOLEAN
    `days the other residences were owned and used` IS A NUMBER
    `periods of service` IS A LIST OF `Period of service`
    `elects the suspension of the 5-year period` IS A BOOLEAN
    `an election is in effect for another property` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the election has been revoked` IS A BOOLEAN
    `dates of other sales or exchanges to which subsection (a) applied` IS A LIST OF DATE
    `subject to the treatment provided by section 877(a)(1)` IS A BOOLEAN

-- What is stated about the sale or exchange itself.
DECLARE `Sale facts` HAS
    `date of the sale or exchange` IS A DATE
    `event in respect of the property` IS AN `Event in respect of the property`
    `the gain` IS A NUMBER
    `a husband and wife make a joint return for the taxable year of the sale or exchange` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the taxpayer` IS AN `Individual facts`
    `the spouse` IS AN `Individual facts`
    `periods a spouse or former spouse used the property as the principal residence, apart from the taxpayer's own` IS A LIST OF Span
    `the taxpayer elects not to have section 121 apply` IS A BOOLEAN
    `acquired in an exchange with respect to which gain is not recognized under section 1031` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the seller is the taxpayer or a person whose basis is determined by reference to the taxpayer's` IS A BOOLEAN
    `date of the acquisition in the exchange` IS A DATE
    `the interest sold is a remainder interest` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the taxpayer elects under subsection (d)(8)(A)` IS A BOOLEAN
    `another interest in the residence is sold or exchanged separately` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the sale is to a person related to the taxpayer as described in section 267(b) or 707(b)` IS A BOOLEAN
    `depreciation adjustments` IS A LIST OF `Depreciation adjustment`
    `temporary absences` IS A LIST OF `Temporary absence`
    `the sale is by reason of a change in place of employment` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the sale is by reason of health` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the sale is by reason of unforeseen circumstances, to the extent provided in regulations` IS A BOOLEAN

-- Whether section 121 reaches the sale at all.
DECLARE `Whether section 121 reaches the sale` IS ONE OF
    `Section 121 applies`
    `Section 121 does not apply because` HAS `the provision` IS A STRING
    `Not covered because` HAS `the reason` IS A STRING

-- Everything the section works out about the gain, with each step kept so that a reader can see what stopped or reduced the exclusion.
DECLARE `How section 121 treats the gain` HAS
    `whether section 121 reaches the sale` IS A `Whether section 121 reaches the sale`
    `the requirements of subsection (a) are met, with (d)(1) and (b)(3)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
    `subsection (c) applies` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
    `the limitation before any reduction under (c)(1)` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
    `the limitation applied` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
    `the gain to which subsection (d)(6) applies` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
    `the gain allocated to periods of nonqualified use` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
    `the gain eligible for exclusion` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
    `the amount excluded` IS A MAYBE NUMBER

§ `Building the facts`

-- Not rules: constructors.
-- The language of the stable binary has no record update, so a fact is stated by filling every field of the record.
-- `the facts of an individual` takes every field in the order of `Individual facts`; the shorter constructors after it fill the rest with "none".
@ref 26 U.S.C. s 121(a) (src:14)
GIVEN holding IS A Holding
      `unmarried, spouse deceased` IS A BOOLEAN
      `deceased spouse's holding` IS A Holding
      `date of death` IS A DATE
      `deceased spouse's other sales` IS A LIST OF DATE
      `received under section 1041(a)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `transferor's periods of ownership` IS A LIST OF Span
      `uses granted` IS A LIST OF `Use granted`
      `cooperative stockholder` IS A BOOLEAN
      `periods of holding the stock` IS A LIST OF Span
      `periods of occupying` IS A LIST OF Span
      `basis under section 1033(b)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `converted holding` IS A Holding
      `incapable of self-care` IS A BOOLEAN
      stays IS A LIST OF `Stay in a facility`
      `section 1034 rollover` IS A BOOLEAN
      `rollover days` IS A NUMBER
      services IS A LIST OF `Period of service`
      elects IS A BOOLEAN
      `other election` IS A BOOLEAN
      revoked IS A BOOLEAN
      `other sales` IS A LIST OF DATE
      `section 877(a)(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH AN `Individual facts`
`the facts of an individual` MEANS
    `Individual facts` WITH
        `holding of the property` IS holding
        `unmarried, spouse deceased on the date of the sale or exchange` IS `unmarried, spouse deceased`
        `deceased spouse's holding of the property` IS `deceased spouse's holding`
        `date of the spouse's death` IS `date of death`
        `deceased spouse's dates of other sales or exchanges to which subsection (a) applied` IS `deceased spouse's other sales`
        `property received in a transaction described in section 1041(a)` IS `received under section 1041(a)`
        `the transferor's periods of ownership` IS `transferor's periods of ownership`
        `uses granted to a spouse or former spouse` IS `uses granted`
        `tenant-stockholder in a cooperative housing corporation` IS `cooperative stockholder`
        `periods of holding the stock` IS `periods of holding the stock`
        `periods of occupying the house or apartment` IS `periods of occupying`
        `basis of the property sold determined under section 1033(b)` IS `basis under section 1033(b)`
        `holding of the converted property` IS `converted holding`
        `became physically or mentally incapable of self-care` IS `incapable of self-care`
        `stays in facilities` IS stays
        `acquired under section 1034 in a rollover` IS `section 1034 rollover`
        `days the other residences were owned and used` IS `rollover days`
        `periods of service` IS services
        `elects the suspension of the 5-year period` IS elects
        `an election is in effect for another property` IS `other election`
        `the election has been revoked` IS revoked
        `dates of other sales or exchanges to which subsection (a) applied` IS `other sales`
        `subject to the treatment provided by section 877(a)(1)` IS `section 877(a)(1)`

-- An individual with only the periods of owning and using the property, and the dates of earlier sales to which subsection (a) applied.
@ref 26 U.S.C. s 121(a) (src:14)
GIVEN owned IS A LIST OF Span
      used IS A LIST OF Span
      `other sales` IS A LIST OF DATE
GIVETH AN `Individual facts`
`an individual who only owned and used the property` MEANS
    `the facts of an individual` (Holding OF owned, used) FALSE (Holding OF EMPTY, EMPTY) (Date 1 1 1900) EMPTY FALSE EMPTY EMPTY FALSE EMPTY EMPTY FALSE (Holding OF EMPTY, EMPTY) FALSE EMPTY FALSE 0 EMPTY FALSE FALSE FALSE `other sales` FALSE

-- An unmarried individual whose spouse died before the sale (subsection (b)(4), (d)(2)): the survivor's periods, the late spouse's, and the dates of each one's earlier sales.
@ref 26 U.S.C. s 121(b)(4), (d)(2) (src:29-30, 69-70)
GIVEN owned IS A LIST OF Span
      used IS A LIST OF Span
      `other sales` IS A LIST OF DATE
      `deceased spouse's holding` IS A Holding
      `date of death` IS A DATE
      `deceased spouse's other sales` IS A LIST OF DATE
GIVETH AN `Individual facts`
`a surviving spouse who owned and used the property` MEANS
    `the facts of an individual` (Holding OF owned, used) TRUE `deceased spouse's holding` `date of death` `deceased spouse's other sales` FALSE EMPTY EMPTY FALSE EMPTY EMPTY FALSE (Holding OF EMPTY, EMPTY) FALSE EMPTY FALSE 0 EMPTY FALSE FALSE FALSE `other sales` FALSE

-- Every field of `Sale facts`, in the order of the record.
@ref 26 U.S.C. s 121(a) (src:13-14)
GIVEN sale IS A DATE
      event IS AN `Event in respect of the property`
      gain IS A NUMBER
      `joint return` IS A BOOLEAN
      taxpayer IS AN `Individual facts`
      spouse IS AN `Individual facts`
      `used by a spouse or former spouse` IS A LIST OF Span
      `elects not under (f)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `like-kind exchange` IS A BOOLEAN
      `seller is the taxpayer` IS A BOOLEAN
      acquisition IS A DATE
      `remainder interest` IS A BOOLEAN
      `elects under (d)(8)(A)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `another interest sold separately` IS A BOOLEAN
      `related person` IS A BOOLEAN
      adjustments IS A LIST OF `Depreciation adjustment`
      absences IS A LIST OF `Temporary absence`
      employment IS A BOOLEAN
      health IS A BOOLEAN
      unforeseen IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Sale facts`
`the facts of a sale` MEANS
    `Sale facts` WITH
        `date of the sale or exchange` IS sale
        `event in respect of the property` IS event
        `the gain` IS gain
        `a husband and wife make a joint return for the taxable year of the sale or exchange` IS `joint return`
        `the taxpayer` IS taxpayer
        `the spouse` IS spouse
        `periods a spouse or former spouse used the property as the principal residence, apart from the taxpayer's own` IS `used by a spouse or former spouse`
        `the taxpayer elects not to have section 121 apply` IS `elects not under (f)`
        `acquired in an exchange with respect to which gain is not recognized under section 1031` IS `like-kind exchange`
        `the seller is the taxpayer or a person whose basis is determined by reference to the taxpayer's` IS `seller is the taxpayer`
        `date of the acquisition in the exchange` IS acquisition
        `the interest sold is a remainder interest` IS `remainder interest`
        `the taxpayer elects under subsection (d)(8)(A)` IS `elects under (d)(8)(A)`
        `another interest in the residence is sold or exchanged separately` IS `another interest sold separately`
        `the sale is to a person related to the taxpayer as described in section 267(b) or 707(b)` IS `related person`
        `depreciation adjustments` IS adjustments
        `temporary absences` IS absences
        `the sale is by reason of a change in place of employment` IS employment
        `the sale is by reason of health` IS health
        `the sale is by reason of unforeseen circumstances, to the extent provided in regulations` IS unforeseen

-- A sale of a home by one taxpayer, or by a couple on a joint return, with none of the special gates.
@ref 26 U.S.C. s 121(a) (src:13-14)
GIVEN sale IS A DATE
      gain IS A NUMBER
      `joint return` IS A BOOLEAN
      taxpayer IS AN `Individual facts`
      spouse IS AN `Individual facts`
      adjustments IS A LIST OF `Depreciation adjustment`
      employment IS A BOOLEAN
      health IS A BOOLEAN
      unforeseen IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Sale facts`
`the usual facts of a sale of a home` MEANS
    `the facts of a sale` sale `sale or exchange` gain `joint return` taxpayer spouse EMPTY FALSE FALSE FALSE (Date 1 1 1900) FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE adjustments EMPTY employment health unforeseen

§ `Gathering each individual's holding: subsections (d)(2) to (d)(7), (g) and (d)(9)`

-- A rule that "includes" periods answers JUST the periods, or NOTHING when its condition fails; the periods it adds are none when it answers NOTHING.
GIVEN m IS A MAYBE (LIST OF Span)
GIVETH A LIST OF Span
`the periods a rule adds, if any` MEANS
    CONSIDER m
    WHEN NOTHING THEN EMPTY
    WHEN JUST ss THEN ss

-- (d)(9)(A), (d)(12): the 5-year period, extended where the individual elects and the election holds.
-- Where no election is shown to hold, the period is the one subsection (a) itself gives.
-- The election is the individual's own, but the days it suspends are those on which "such individual or such individual's spouse is serving" (lines 108 and 146),
-- so the service of the spouse counts as well, on a joint return or not (fork F30); `partner` is the individual's spouse, and a person with no spouse states none.
@ref 26 U.S.C. s 121(d)(9)(A) and (B), (d)(12) (src:107-113)
GIVEN person IS AN `Individual facts`
      partner IS AN `Individual facts`
      sale IS A DATE
GIVETH A Span
`s 121(a), (d)(9) and (d)(12) the period for the individual, as extended by an election that holds` MEANS
    IF `s 121(d)(9)(A) the running of the 5-year period is suspended at the individual's election` (person's `elects the suspension of the 5-year period`) (person's `an election is in effect for another property`) (person's `the election has been revoked`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN `s 121(d)(9)(B) the 5-year period as extended, by no more than 10 years` sale (`s 121(d)(9)(A) and (d)(12)(A) the days of service that suspend the 5-year period` (append (person's `periods of service`) (partner's `periods of service`)))
    ELSE `s 121(a) the 5-year period ending on the date of the sale or exchange` sale

-- (d)(2) to (d)(5)(C) add periods of owning; (d)(2), (d)(3)(B), (d)(4)(B), (d)(5)(C) and (d)(7) add periods of use.
@ref 26 U.S.C. s 121(d)(2) to (d)(7) (src:69-99)
GIVEN person IS AN `Individual facts`
      window IS A Span
      sale IS A DATE
GIVETH A Holding
`s 121(d) the individual's holding with the special rules of subsection (d) applied` MEANS
    Holding OF ownedAll, usedAll
    WHERE
        own MEANS person's `holding of the property`
        deceased MEANS person's `deceased spouse's holding of the property`
        dateBeforeDeath MEANS person's `date of the spouse's death`
        converted MEANS `s 121(d)(5)(C) the holding and use of the converted property are treated as holding and use of the property sold` (person's `basis of the property sold determined under section 1033(b)`) (person's `holding of the converted property`)
        convertedOwned MEANS
            CONSIDER converted
            WHEN NOTHING THEN EMPTY
            WHEN JUST h THEN h's `periods of ownership`
        convertedUsed MEANS
            CONSIDER converted
            WHEN NOTHING THEN EMPTY
            WHEN JUST h THEN h's `periods of use as the principal residence`
        ownedAll MEANS
            `the spans with no day counted twice`
                (concat (LIST
                      (own's `periods of ownership`)
                    , `the periods a rule adds, if any` (`s 121(d)(2) the periods the deceased spouse owned the property before death are included` (person's `unmarried, spouse deceased on the date of the sale or exchange`) (deceased's `periods of ownership`) dateBeforeDeath)
                    , `the periods a rule adds, if any` (`s 121(d)(3)(A) the period the transferor owned the property is included` (person's `property received in a transaction described in section 1041(a)`) (person's `the transferor's periods of ownership`))
                    , `the periods a rule adds, if any` (`s 121(d)(4)(A) the holding requirement is applied to the holding of the stock` (person's `tenant-stockholder in a cooperative housing corporation`) (person's `periods of holding the stock`))
                    , convertedOwned))
        usedBeforeDeemed MEANS
            `the spans with no day counted twice`
                (concat (LIST
                      (own's `periods of use as the principal residence`)
                    , `the periods a rule adds, if any` (`s 121(d)(2) the periods the deceased spouse used the property before death are included` (person's `unmarried, spouse deceased on the date of the sale or exchange`) (deceased's `periods of use as the principal residence`) dateBeforeDeath)
                    , `the periods a rule adds, if any` (`s 121(d)(3)(B) the individual is treated as using the property as the principal residence while a spouse or former spouse is granted use` ownedAll (person's `uses granted to a spouse or former spouse`))
                    , `the periods a rule adds, if any` (`s 121(d)(4)(B) the use requirement is applied to the house or apartment the taxpayer was entitled to occupy` (person's `tenant-stockholder in a cooperative housing corporation`) (person's `periods of occupying the house or apartment`))
                    , convertedUsed))
        usedAll MEANS
            `the spans with no day counted twice`
                (append usedBeforeDeemed
                    (`the periods a rule adds, if any` (`s 121(d)(7) the taxpayer is treated as using the property as the principal residence while residing in a licensed facility` (person's `became physically or mentally incapable of self-care`) (Holding OF ownedAll, usedBeforeDeemed) window sale (person's `stays in facilities`))))

-- (g): the days the earlier residences were owned and used, added to the days owned and to the days used.
@ref 26 U.S.C. s 121(g) (src:155-156)
GIVEN person IS AN `Individual facts`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 121(g) the days added for the individual` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 121(g) the days the other residence was owned and used are included` (person's `acquired under section 1034 in a rollover`) (person's `days the other residences were owned and used`)
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): when subsection (g)'s condition fails it adds no days.
    WHEN NOTHING THEN 0
    WHEN JUST n THEN n

§ `Each individual's requirements and bar`

@ref 26 U.S.C. s 121(a) (src:14)
GIVEN person IS AN `Individual facts`
      partner IS AN `Individual facts`
      sale IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 121(a) the individual meets the ownership requirement` MEANS
    `s 121(a) the ownership requirement is met` (holding's `periods of ownership`) window sale (`s 121(g) the days added for the individual` person)
    WHERE
        window MEANS `s 121(a), (d)(9) and (d)(12) the period for the individual, as extended by an election that holds` person partner sale
        holding MEANS `s 121(d) the individual's holding with the special rules of subsection (d) applied` person window sale

@ref 26 U.S.C. s 121(a) (src:14)
GIVEN person IS AN `Individual facts`
      partner IS AN `Individual facts`
      sale IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 121(a) the individual meets the use requirement` MEANS
    `s 121(a) the use requirement is met` (holding's `periods of use as the principal residence`) window sale (`s 121(g) the days added for the individual` person)
    WHERE
        window MEANS `s 121(a), (d)(9) and (d)(12) the period for the individual, as extended by an election that holds` person partner sale
        holding MEANS `s 121(d) the individual's holding with the special rules of subsection (d) applied` person window sale

@ref 26 U.S.C. s 121(a) (src:14)
GIVEN person IS AN `Individual facts`
      partner IS AN `Individual facts`
      sale IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 121(a) the individual meets the ownership and use requirements` MEANS
    `both are true` (`s 121(a) the individual meets the ownership requirement` person partner sale) (`s 121(a) the individual meets the use requirement` person partner sale)

-- (b)(2)(B), second sentence: "each spouse shall be treated as owning the property during the period that either spouse owned the property."
@ref 26 U.S.C. s 121(b)(2)(B) (src:26)
GIVEN person IS AN `Individual facts`
      other IS AN `Individual facts`
      sale IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 121(b)(2)(B) the individual meets the ownership requirement, treated as owning the property when either spouse owned it` MEANS
    `s 121(a) the ownership requirement is met` bothOwned window sale (`s 121(g) the days added for the individual` person)
    WHERE
        window MEANS `s 121(a), (d)(9) and (d)(12) the period for the individual, as extended by an election that holds` person other sale
        mine MEANS (`s 121(d) the individual's holding with the special rules of subsection (d) applied` person window sale)'s `periods of ownership`
        theirs MEANS (`s 121(d) the individual's holding with the special rules of subsection (d) applied` other (`s 121(a), (d)(9) and (d)(12) the period for the individual, as extended by an election that holds` other person sale) sale)'s `periods of ownership`
        bothOwned MEANS `the spans of both lists` mine theirs

@ref 26 U.S.C. s 121(b)(3) (src:27-28)
GIVEN person IS AN `Individual facts`
      sale IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 121(b)(3) the individual is barred by another sale or exchange within 2 years` MEANS
    `s 121(b)(3) subsection (a) shall not apply because of another sale or exchange within 2 years` sale (person's `dates of other sales or exchanges to which subsection (a) applied`)

§ `The gates: whether section 121 reaches the sale`

-- (d)(5)(A): the event is treated as the sale; a sale or exchange needs no such rule.
@ref 26 U.S.C. s 121(d)(5)(A) (src:87-88)
GIVEN event IS AN `Event in respect of the property`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 121(d)(5)(A) the event counts as a sale or exchange for this section` MEANS
    CONSIDER event
    WHEN `sale or exchange` THEN JUST TRUE
    OTHERWISE `s 121(d)(5)(A) the event is treated as the sale of the property` event

@ref 26 U.S.C. s 121(d)(5)(A), (d)(8), (d)(10), (e), (f) (src:87-88)
GIVEN facts IS A `Sale facts`
GIVETH A `Whether section 121 reaches the sale`
`s 121 whether the section reaches the sale or exchange` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `s 121(d)(5)(A) the event counts as a sale or exchange for this section` (facts's `event in respect of the property`) EQUALS NOTHING THEN
            `Not covered because` "the event is not one the text treats as a sale or exchange: subsection (d)(5)(A) lists destruction, theft, seizure, requisition and condemnation without closing the list"
        IF `s 121(e) this section applies to the sale or exchange by the individual` (taxpayer's `subject to the treatment provided by section 877(a)(1)`) EQUALS JUST FALSE THEN
            `Section 121 does not apply because` "subsection (e): the treatment provided by section 877(a)(1) applies to the taxpayer"
        IF facts's `a husband and wife make a joint return for the taxable year of the sale or exchange` AND (spouse's `subject to the treatment provided by section 877(a)(1)`) THEN
            `Not covered because` "subsection (e) speaks of a sale by an individual to whom section 877(a)(1) applies; it does not say what that does to a joint return of that individual's spouse"
        IF `s 121(f) this section applies to the sale or exchange` (facts's `the taxpayer elects not to have section 121 apply`) EQUALS JUST FALSE THEN
            `Section 121 does not apply because` "subsection (f): the taxpayer elects not to have this section apply"
        IF `s 121(d)(10) subsection (a) shall not apply to the sale of property acquired in a like-kind exchange` (facts's `acquired in an exchange with respect to which gain is not recognized under section 1031`) (facts's `the seller is the taxpayer or a person whose basis is determined by reference to the taxpayer's`) (facts's `date of the acquisition in the exchange`) (facts's `date of the sale or exchange`) EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN
            `Section 121 does not apply because` "subsection (d)(10): the property was acquired in a like-kind exchange less than 5 years before the sale"
        IF facts's `the interest sold is a remainder interest` AND (`s 121(d)(8)(B) subparagraph (A) applies to the sale` (facts's `the sale is to a person related to the taxpayer as described in section 267(b) or 707(b)`) EQUALS JUST FALSE) THEN
            `Not covered because` "subsection (d)(8)(B) takes the election of (d)(8)(A) away for a sale to a related person, and the text does not say that section 121 then fails to apply to a remainder interest"
        IF facts's `the interest sold is a remainder interest` AND NOT (`s 121(d)(8)(A) this section does not fail to apply to the sale of the interest by reason of its being a remainder interest` (facts's `the interest sold is a remainder interest`) (facts's `the taxpayer elects under subsection (d)(8)(A)`) (facts's `another interest in the residence is sold or exchanged separately`) EQUALS JUST TRUE) THEN
            `Not covered because` "subsection (d)(8)(A) protects a remainder interest only at the taxpayer's election, and the text does not say that section 121 fails to apply without it"
        IF `s 121(d)(8)(A) this section does not fail to apply to the sale of the interest by reason of its being a remainder interest` (facts's `the interest sold is a remainder interest`) (facts's `the taxpayer elects under subsection (d)(8)(A)`) (facts's `another interest in the residence is sold or exchanged separately`) EQUALS JUST FALSE THEN
            `Section 121 does not apply because` "subsection (d)(8)(A): section 121 does not apply to another interest in the residence sold or exchanged separately"
        OTHERWISE `Section 121 applies`
    WHERE
        taxpayer MEANS facts's `the taxpayer`
        spouse MEANS facts's `the spouse`

§ `The limitation: subsections (b)(1), (b)(2), (b)(4) and (c)(1)`

-- Joint return: (b)(2)(A), else (b)(2)(B). Not a joint return: (b)(4) for a surviving spouse, else (b)(1).
@ref 26 U.S.C. s 121(b)(1), (b)(2), (b)(4) (src:16-30)
GIVEN facts IS A `Sale facts`
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 121(b) the limitation before any reduction under (c)(1)` MEANS
    IF `a joint return`
    THEN CONSIDER limbsA
         WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
         WHEN JUST yes THEN
             IF yes
             THEN `s 121(b)(2)(A) the limitation under paragraph (1) as substituted` (JUST TRUE)
             ELSE `s 121(b)(2)(B) the limitation for other joint returns` `a joint return` (JUST FALSE) entitledTaxpayer entitledSpouse
    ELSE IF taxpayer's `unmarried, spouse deceased on the date of the sale or exchange`
         THEN CONSIDER survivor
              WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
              WHEN JUST yes THEN
                  IF yes
                  THEN JUST 500_000
                  -- paragraph (1) as written: "shall not exceed $250,000"
                  ELSE JUST (`s 121(b)(1) the dollar limitation`)
         ELSE JUST (`s 121(b)(1) the dollar limitation`)
    WHERE
        `a joint return` MEANS facts's `a husband and wife make a joint return for the taxable year of the sale or exchange`
        sale MEANS facts's `date of the sale or exchange`
        taxpayer MEANS facts's `the taxpayer`
        spouse MEANS facts's `the spouse`
        limbsA MEANS `s 121(b)(2)(A) paragraph (1) is applied by substituting $500,000 for $250,000` `a joint return` limbI limbII limbIII
        limbI MEANS `s 121(b)(2)(A)(i) either spouse meets the ownership requirements of subsection (a)` (`s 121(a) the individual meets the ownership requirement` taxpayer spouse sale) (`s 121(a) the individual meets the ownership requirement` spouse taxpayer sale)
        limbII MEANS `s 121(b)(2)(A)(ii) both spouses meet the use requirements of subsection (a)` (`s 121(a) the individual meets the use requirement` taxpayer spouse sale) (`s 121(a) the individual meets the use requirement` spouse taxpayer sale)
        limbIII MEANS `s 121(b)(2)(A)(iii) neither spouse is ineligible by reason of paragraph (3)` (`s 121(b)(3) the individual is barred by another sale or exchange within 2 years` taxpayer sale) (`s 121(b)(3) the individual is barred by another sale or exchange within 2 years` spouse sale)
        entitledTaxpayer MEANS `s 121(b)(2)(B) the limitation under paragraph (1) to which the spouse would be entitled if the spouses had not been married` (`s 121(b)(2)(B) the individual meets the ownership requirement, treated as owning the property when either spouse owned it` taxpayer spouse sale) (`s 121(a) the individual meets the use requirement` taxpayer spouse sale) (`s 121(b)(3) the individual is barred by another sale or exchange within 2 years` taxpayer sale)
        entitledSpouse MEANS `s 121(b)(2)(B) the limitation under paragraph (1) to which the spouse would be entitled if the spouses had not been married` (`s 121(b)(2)(B) the individual meets the ownership requirement, treated as owning the property when either spouse owned it` spouse taxpayer sale) (`s 121(a) the individual meets the use requirement` spouse taxpayer sale) (`s 121(b)(3) the individual is barred by another sale or exchange within 2 years` spouse sale)
        survivor MEANS `s 121(b)(4) paragraph (1) is applied by substituting $500,000 for $250,000` TRUE sale (taxpayer's `date of the spouse's death`) survivorRequirements
        survivorRequirements MEANS `s 121(b)(4) the requirements of paragraph (2)(A) were met immediately before the date of death` (taxpayer's `holding of the property`) (taxpayer's `deceased spouse's holding of the property`) (taxpayer's `date of the spouse's death`) (taxpayer's `dates of other sales or exchanges to which subsection (a) applied`) (taxpayer's `deceased spouse's dates of other sales or exchanges to which subsection (a) applied`)

§ `The treatment of the gain`

-- The smaller of two answers, where both are given; NOTHING if either is not covered.
GIVEN a IS A MAYBE NUMBER
      b IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`the smaller of two answers` MEANS
    CONSIDER a
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST x THEN
        CONSIDER b
        WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
        WHEN JUST y THEN JUST (`the smaller of` x y)

@ref 26 U.S.C. s 121 (src:13-156)
GIVEN facts IS A `Sale facts`
GIVETH A `How section 121 treats the gain`
`s 121 the treatment of the gain from the sale or exchange` MEANS
    `How section 121 treats the gain` WITH
        `whether section 121 reaches the sale` IS gate
        `the requirements of subsection (a) are met, with (d)(1) and (b)(3)` IS routeA
        `subsection (c) applies` IS routeC
        `the limitation before any reduction under (c)(1)` IS limitBefore
        `the limitation applied` IS limitApplied
        `the gain to which subsection (d)(6) applies` IS d6
        `the gain allocated to periods of nonqualified use` IS allocated
        `the gain eligible for exclusion` IS eligible
        `the amount excluded` IS excluded
    WHERE
        sale MEANS facts's `date of the sale or exchange`
        gain MEANS facts's `the gain`
        `a joint return` MEANS facts's `a husband and wife make a joint return for the taxable year of the sale or exchange`
        taxpayer MEANS facts's `the taxpayer`
        spouse MEANS facts's `the spouse`
        gate MEANS `s 121 whether the section reaches the sale or exchange` facts

        -- the route
        requirementsT MEANS `s 121(a) the individual meets the ownership and use requirements` taxpayer spouse sale
        requirementsS MEANS `s 121(a) the individual meets the ownership and use requirements` spouse taxpayer sale
        barT MEANS `s 121(b)(3) the individual is barred by another sale or exchange within 2 years` taxpayer sale
        routeA MEANS
            IF `a joint return`
            THEN `s 121(d)(1) subsections (a) and (c) apply to the joint return` TRUE requirementsT requirementsS
            ELSE `both are true` requirementsT (`the opposite of` barT)
        reasonB MEANS `s 121(c)(2)(B) the sale is by reason of a change in place of employment, health, or unforeseen circumstances` (facts's `the sale is by reason of a change in place of employment`) (facts's `the sale is by reason of health`) (facts's `the sale is by reason of unforeseen circumstances, to the extent provided in regulations`)
        routeC MEANS
            IF `a joint return`
            -- NOTHING-kind (silent): on a joint return the text does not say whose periods measure the shorter period of (c)(1)(B)(i) (fork F17), so the (c) route is answered only where the reason fails.
            THEN (IF reasonB EQUALS JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE ELSE NOTHING)
            ELSE `s 121(c)(2) this subsection applies to the sale or exchange` (`s 121(c)(2)(A) subsection (a) would not (but for this subsection) apply by reason of (i) or (ii)` (`s 121(c)(2)(A)(i) subsection (a) would not apply by reason of a failure to meet the ownership and use requirements` requirementsT) (`s 121(c)(2)(A)(ii) subsection (a) would not apply by reason of subsection (b)(3)` barT)) reasonB

        -- the limitation
        limitBefore MEANS `s 121(b) the limitation before any reduction under (c)(1)` facts
        taxpayerWindow MEANS `s 121(a), (d)(9) and (d)(12) the period for the individual, as extended by an election that holds` taxpayer spouse sale
        taxpayerHolding MEANS `s 121(d) the individual's holding with the special rules of subsection (d) applied` taxpayer taxpayerWindow sale
        shorter MEANS `s 121(c)(1)(B)(i) the shorter of (I) and (II)` (`s 121(c)(1)(B)(i)(I) the aggregate periods during the 5-year period the property has been owned and used as the principal residence` taxpayerHolding taxpayerWindow) (`s 121(c)(1)(B)(i)(II) the period after the most recent prior sale or exchange and before the date of such sale` sale (taxpayer's `dates of other sales or exchanges to which subsection (a) applied`))
        reducedLimit MEANS
            CONSIDER limitBefore
            WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
            WHEN JUST l THEN JUST (`s 121(c)(1) the dollar limitation as reduced` l shorter (`s 121(c)(1)(B)(ii) 2 years, counted in days, ending on the date of the sale or exchange` sale))
        limitApplied MEANS
            BRANCH
                IF routeA EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN limitBefore
                IF routeC EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN reducedLimit
                -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Gross income shall not include gain from the sale or exchange of property if ..." (subsection (a)'s "if" fails and subsection (c) does not apply either; marginal reading (a)): nothing can be excluded, so the limitation is $0.
                IF routeA EQUALS JUST FALSE AND routeC EQUALS JUST FALSE THEN JUST 0
                -- NOTHING-kind (silent): when a route's answer is not given there is no limitation to apply.
                OTHERWISE NOTHING

        -- the gain: (d)(6) first, then (b)(5), as (b)(5)(D) orders
        d6 MEANS `s 121(d)(6) the gain to which subsection (a) shall not apply` gain (facts's `depreciation adjustments`)
        gainAfterD6 MEANS
            CONSIDER d6
            WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
            WHEN JUST x THEN JUST (`s 121(b)(5)(D)(i) the gain to which subparagraph (A) is applied after the application of subsection (d)(6)` gain x)
        gainForRatio MEANS
            CONSIDER d6
            WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
            WHEN JUST x THEN JUST (`s 121(b)(5)(D)(ii) the gain to which subparagraph (B) is applied, without regard to the gain to which (d)(6) applies` gain x)
        ownedByTaxpayer MEANS (taxpayerHolding)'s `periods of ownership`
        ownedBySpouse MEANS
            IF `a joint return`
            THEN (`s 121(d) the individual's holding with the special rules of subsection (d) applied` spouse (`s 121(a), (d)(9) and (d)(12) the period for the individual, as extended by an election that holds` spouse taxpayer sale) sale)'s `periods of ownership`
            ELSE EMPTY
        usedBySpouse MEANS
            IF `a joint return`
            THEN (`s 121(d) the individual's holding with the special rules of subsection (d) applied` spouse (`s 121(a), (d)(9) and (d)(12) the period for the individual, as extended by an election that holds` spouse taxpayer sale) sale)'s `periods of use as the principal residence`
            ELSE EMPTY
        ownedTogether MEANS `the spans with no day counted twice` (append ownedByTaxpayer ownedBySpouse)
        usedTogether MEANS `the spans with no day counted twice` (concat (LIST (taxpayerHolding's `periods of use as the principal residence`), usedBySpouse, (facts's `periods a spouse or former spouse used the property as the principal residence, apart from the taxpayer's own`)))
        -- "the taxpayer or the taxpayer's spouse is serving" (line 45): the spouse's service counts on any return (fork F30).
        dutyDays MEANS `s 121(d)(9)(A) the days of service on qualified official extended duty described in clause (i), (ii) or (iii)` (append (taxpayer's `periods of service`) (spouse's `periods of service`))
        nonqualifiedDays MEANS `s 121(b)(5)(C) the aggregate days of nonqualified use` ownedTogether usedTogether usedTogether taxpayerWindow sale dutyDays (facts's `temporary absences`)
        ratio MEANS `s 121(b)(5)(B) the ratio of the aggregate periods of nonqualified use to the period owned` nonqualifiedDays (`the days in the spans of a list` ownedTogether)
        allocated MEANS
            CONSIDER gainForRatio
            WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
            WHEN JUST g THEN `s 121(b)(5)(A) the gain to which subsection (a) shall not apply, being the gain allocated to periods of nonqualified use` g ratio
        eligible MEANS
            CONSIDER gainAfterD6
            WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
            WHEN JUST g THEN
                CONSIDER allocated
                WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
                WHEN JUST a THEN JUST (g MINUS a)

        -- the amount: "shall not exceed" the limitation
        excluded MEANS
            CONSIDER gate
            WHEN `Section 121 does not apply because` why THEN JUST 0
            WHEN `Not covered because` why THEN NOTHING
            WHEN `Section 121 applies` THEN
                BRANCH
                    -- NOTHING-kind (silent): section 121 speaks of "gain"; a loss is not a case it addresses.
                    IF gain LESS THAN 0 THEN NOTHING
                    IF routeA EQUALS JUST TRUE OR routeC EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN `the smaller of two answers` eligible limitApplied
                    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Gross income shall not include gain from the sale or exchange of property if, during the 5-year period ..." (the "if" fails and subsection (c) does not apply either; marginal reading (a))
                    IF routeA EQUALS JUST FALSE AND routeC EQUALS JUST FALSE THEN JUST 0
                    OTHERWISE NOTHING

@ref 26 U.S.C. s 121(a) (src:13-14)
GIVEN facts IS A `Sale facts`
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 121 the amount of the gain excluded from gross income` MEANS
    (`s 121 the treatment of the gain from the sale or exchange` facts)'s `the amount excluded`

@ref 26 U.S.C. s 121(a) (src:13-14)
GIVEN facts IS A `Sale facts`
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 121 the amount of the gain that stays in gross income` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 121 the amount of the gain excluded from gross income` facts
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST x THEN JUST (facts's `the gain` MINUS x)

-- What stopped or reduced the exclusion, one line per provision that did.
@ref 26 U.S.C. s 121 (src:13-156)
GIVEN facts IS A `Sale facts`
GIVETH A LIST OF STRING
`s 121 what stops or reduces the exclusion` MEANS
    CONSIDER t's `whether section 121 reaches the sale`
    WHEN `Section 121 does not apply because` why THEN LIST why
    WHEN `Not covered because` why THEN LIST (CONCAT "not covered: ", why)
    WHEN `Section 121 applies` THEN concat (LIST routeLines, limitLines, gainLines)
    WHERE
        t MEANS `s 121 the treatment of the gain from the sale or exchange` facts
        routeLines MEANS
            IF t's `the requirements of subsection (a) are met, with (d)(1) and (b)(3)` EQUALS JUST FALSE
            THEN (IF t's `subsection (c) applies` EQUALS JUST TRUE
                  THEN LIST "subsection (a) does not apply, but subsection (c) reduces the limitation"
                  ELSE LIST "subsection (a): the ownership and use requirements are not met, or subsection (b)(3) bars the sale, and subsection (c) does not rescue it")
            ELSE EMPTY
        -- Only where a route applies: when neither does, the limitation of $0 is not what held the gain back.
        limitLines MEANS
            IF NOT (t's `the requirements of subsection (a) are met, with (d)(1) and (b)(3)` EQUALS JUST TRUE OR t's `subsection (c) applies` EQUALS JUST TRUE)
            THEN EMPTY
            ELSE CONSIDER t's `the gain eligible for exclusion`
                 WHEN NOTHING THEN EMPTY
                 WHEN JUST e THEN
                     CONSIDER t's `the limitation applied`
                     WHEN NOTHING THEN EMPTY
                     WHEN JUST l THEN IF e GREATER THAN l THEN LIST "subsection (b): the gain left after (d)(6) and (b)(5) is more than the limitation, and the excess stays in gross income" ELSE EMPTY
        gainLines MEANS
            concat (LIST
                  (CONSIDER t's `the gain to which subsection (d)(6) applies`
                   WHEN NOTHING THEN LIST "not covered: subsection (d)(6) does not say how to divide a depreciation adjustment that straddles May 6, 1997"
                   WHEN JUST x THEN IF x GREATER THAN 0 THEN LIST "subsection (d)(6): gain up to the depreciation adjustments attributable to periods after May 6, 1997 is not excluded" ELSE EMPTY)
                , (CONSIDER t's `the gain allocated to periods of nonqualified use`
                   WHEN NOTHING THEN EMPTY
                   WHEN JUST x THEN IF x GREATER THAN 0 THEN LIST "subsection (b)(5): gain allocated to periods of nonqualified use is not excluded" ELSE EMPTY))
